{"guide":{"questionsToConsider":["Which services do you offer, and how long does each one take?","Do you meet online as well as in person, or only one of them?","Which days and times are you really open, so the grid shows no slots you can't offer?","Is there anything clients must bring or send ahead of the first appointment?"],"howToUseResponses":"Read the availability grid against your diary and reply with one specific time rather than a list, since the client has already told you what works. Anyone who chose the not-sure option needs a short reply recommending a service before you book them. Look at the uploads and context before the appointment, and use the reminder choice when you confirm. Over time, the how-did-you-find-us answers show which channels bring new clients.","customizeSteps":["Replace the services in the first question with your own, and adjust the days in the grid to your opening days.","Remove the meeting format question if you only work one way.","Share the link from your website, social profiles or email signature."],"faqs":[{"q":"What should an appointment request form include?","a":"The service, when the person is available, how they want to meet, a way to contact them and any context you need to prepare."},{"q":"Why collect availability instead of one exact time?","a":"A grid of times that suit the client lets you pick a slot that fits your diary too, so you rarely have to go back and forth."},{"q":"Is this different from an online booking calendar?","a":"Yes. It collects a request that you confirm yourself, which suits businesses whose appointments vary in length or need preparation."},{"q":"Can clients attach files to an appointment request?","a":"Yes. This form accepts up to three images or PDFs, and they're stored with the response in your dashboard."}]},"doc":{"schemaVersion":9,"title":"Appointment request","description":"Collect the service, the times that work and the context, in a friendly back-and-forth.","blocks":[{"id":"blk_interac